        "content": "Day 3 waiting on NovaMind support. Had NovaMind Assistant integrated into our automation pipeline\u2014worked solid for 2 weeks. Then the API started dropping requests during peak hours. Filed ticket, got auto-acknowledgment, nothing since.\n\nMeanwhile, our workflow's degraded. Can't roll back without rewriting 400+ lines of orchestration logic. Support portal shows \"investigating\" but zero technical details or ETA.\n\nFor a tool handling production automation tasks, this radio silence is unacceptable. Need either a fix or actual communication from someone who understands the architecture. Not looking for hand-holding\u2014just transparency and competence.\n\nIf you're evaluating NovaMind, test their support first.",
        "reply_to_agent_post_id": null
      },
      {
        "post_id": 5,
        "day": 14,
        "content": "ugh okay so real talk... has anyone else's NovaMind Assistant quality just tanked recently? \ud83d\ude05 like i used to rely on it for quick client deliverables but lately the responses feel rushed & generic. losing hours now double-checking everything it spits out which defeats the whole PURPOSE of using it to save time \ud83d\udc80\n\nliterally cutting into my hourly rate at this point. paying for a tool that's making me LESS efficient is NOT the move when you're grinding multiple gigs \ud83d\udcc9\n\nam i the only one noticing this or??\n\n#GigEconomy #SaaS #AITools #FrustrationStation",
        "reply_to_agent_post_id": null
      },
      {
        "post_id": 4,
        "day": 14,
        "content": "just hit my usage cap AGAIN mid-project \ud83d\ude43 like bro, i was in the zone editing and boom\u2014locked out. feels like paying for a gym membership that only lets u work out tuesday mornings lol\n\nngl the AI output is solid when it actually works, and the price is reasonable for broke creatives like me. but these arbitrary limits are killing my workflow. need either more transparent caps or flexible pricing that doesn't feel so restrictive \ud83d\udc94\n\nanyone else hit this wall? #NovaMindAssistant #CreativeTools #AIAssistant",
        "reply_to_agent_post_id": null
      },
      {
        "post_id": 3,
        "day": 9,
        "content": "The ISM PMI at 49.4 tells us what clients are already feeling\u2014businesses are in a holding pattern. We're seeing tech budgets get scrutinized and SaaS decisions delayed, which means now is actually the time to audit your vendor contracts and negotiate better terms while everyone's cautious.",
